  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "The wheel of a bicycle is $70$ cm in diameter.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q14a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Suppose the wheel makes $2$ revolutions per second. Calculate the speed of the cyclist in kilometres per hour, accurate to $2$ decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15.83\\text{ km/h}$.",
          "worked": "$70\\text{ cm}=0.7\\text{ m}$. The distance travelled per revolution is\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\pi d\\\\C&=0.7\\pi\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $2$ revolutions per second,\n$$\\begin{align*}v&=2\\times0.7\\pi\\times\\frac{3600}{1000}\\\\v&=5.04\\pi\\text{ km/h}\\\\v&\\approx15.83\\text{ km/h}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q14b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If the cyclist is travelling at a speed of $40$ kilometres per hour, then how many revolutions per second does the wheel make, accurate to $2$ decimal places?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.05\\text{ rev/s}$.",
          "worked": "The wheel travels $0.7\\pi$ m per revolution. Convert the speed:\n$$\\begin{align*}v&=40\\times\\frac{1000}{3600}\\\\v&=\\frac{100}{9}\\text{ m/s}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe number $n$ of revolutions per second is\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=\\frac{100/9}{0.7\\pi}\\\\n&=\\frac{1000}{63\\pi}\\\\n&\\approx5.05\\text{ rev/s}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
